{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Abraham returned to Beer-sheba.</b> Not an actual 'return' — for he was dwelling in Hebron. Twelve years before the binding of Isaac he had left Beer-sheba and gone to Hebron, as it says ״וַיָּגָר אַבְרָהָם בְּאֶרֶץ פְּלִשְׁתִּים יָמִים רַבִּים״ — 'many days,' more than the first ones in Hebron, and they were twenty-six years, as we explained above."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:58.344228899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}